    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2RF6GW7pGNxip44jJXyc3RD)_\n\nFixes `browse-url-url-at-point: Wrong type argument: buffer-or-string-p, (link ...)` when opening a URL in an Org file.\n\n- `browse-url-url-at-point` calls `(thing-at-point 'url t)`, which strips text properties from whatever the provider returns. A list (a parsed `link` element) there gives exactly this `buffer-or-string-p` error.\n- Org buffers now use `sp-org-url-at-point` as the `url` provider. It always returns a string or nil.\n- A Markdown link pasted inside a plain link (`https://[www.youtube.com/watch?v=x](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=x)`) opens the inner address.\n- Doc section, CHANGELOG line and `tests/sp-org-url-test.el` added.\n\n**Caveat:** I did not find in this repository the code that returns the link object, so the cause is inferred from the error and the `thingatpt` source. The fix guards the answer for Org buffers. If it still fails, `M-x toggle-debug-on-error` and send the backtrace.\n\nNot run in Emacs (none in the container).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiAw3m6imhQss8F11fp)_",
